s  in one week that is a new record over  the record set the week before and each  one of these jobs lost means another  paycheck that's not being spent in the  community that is not circulating  in the economy how can one job loss lead  to even still more and where does this  put us trajectory wise as we look into  the next quarter you know I think that  as we look at economic growth it is gone  it's obviously come to a standstill and  that started as early as the beginning  of March we are obviously in a recession  already we usually only claim a  recession in retrospect but it's clear  from these numbers that we are there we  are seeing economic output estimates  meaning what's gonna happen in the  economy they're all over the place we  just got one out from the Bank of  America of a more than fifteen percent  drop that we could see in the next  quarter we've seen estimates up to 30  percent but what we really are looking  at here is the unknown and I think that  is why economists are all over the place  with these projections we are not  talking about something we've ever seen  before we're talking about something  that is essentially a health pandemic  that is now morphed into an economic  pandemic and there are too many  variables you know when you have  economists talking to epidemics that we  are going to get estimates all over the  world yeah this is all very new there is  no precedent but somebody with a long  memory on this subject who has covered  the economy for years as our Anthony  Mason's let's go to him with a question  Anthony good morning yeah Jill I'm  wondering if you were running a business  right now you obviously you don't know  what to plan for so how do you plan what  do you do well I think that this goes  back to your basics and I've been  talking to a lot of small business  owners specifically and they are saying  look this program for these front  through the Small Business  Administration which opens tomorrow  could be important but the